[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue, one fix queued. The reports say three. They were merged
on subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)), and the subjects all say
"wrong day". What went wrong is in the body, the tenant and the way the report came in.

<Callout kind="warn">
The queued parser fix closes one of the three. The other two keep coming in after it ships.
</Callout>

## What is in #4471

<SplitTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

## parser: the shared parser reads month first

Every tenant on file writes the day first. The shared parser reads month first, so 12/05 becomes
5 December. Reports come in by app, email and the booking-v2 form, from all tenants. This is the
bug #4471 describes, and the fix that is queued.

## hint: booking-v3 tells people to type month first

booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field and then reads the date the tenant's way, day
first. People type what the hint says and get a swapped date. Only reports sent through the form, and
only from tenants on booking-v3. The parser fix does not touch it: the form has to print the
tenant's own order.

Intake tags disagree with this split in both directions; count by tenant and channel, not by
`intakeTag`.

## shift: dates move by one day

These are the reports the desk itself read as a one-day move. A day/month swap cannot do that:
12 May flips to 5 December, never to 11 May. The same meeting shows on different days in Lisbon and
Toronto. This points at time zones (a date stored as midnight in one zone and shown in another),
not at date order.

<ShiftReports />

## What changes on the desk

- Close #4471 for `parser` only when the parser fix ships; `hint` and `shift` stay open on their own tickets.
- Merging on subject alone put three problems under one ticket. Before merging a date report,
  check the tenant's form and channel, and whether the date flipped or moved by a day.

